CoryDora's original hardware designs and accompanying documentation in this
repository are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 -
Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S-2.0). The complete licence text is in
LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-2.0.txt.

This covers original schematics, PCB layouts, project files, fabrication
outputs, bills of materials, enclosure CAD and exports, build instructions,
diagrams, and project photographs whose copyright is held by CoryDora's
contributors, unless a file carries a different explicit licence notice.

Attribution notice: CoryDora project and its contributors.
Source location: https://github.com/balub/CoryDora
Retain applicable copyright, acknowledgement, licence, and source-location
notices when redistributing source or derivatives, as required by the licence.
Identify modifications and provide the Complete Source under CERN-OHL-S-2.0
when required by the licence.

The covered source and products are supplied without warranty, as detailed
in section 6 of the licence.

Third-party material

Third-party components, libraries, footprints, models, datasheets, logos,
and other material retain their existing licences and ownership. This
licence does not relicense material CoryDora's contributors do not own.
Preserve the relevant upstream copyright and licence notices. In particular,
V2/libraries/MX_V2 retains its upstream licence in that directory.

Firmware

CoryDora's QMK-based firmware is maintained separately at
https://github.com/balub/qmk_firmware and retains the applicable licences
in that repository. It is not relicensed by this file.

Names and branding

This licence does not grant trademark rights to the CoryDora name or logos,
or imply endorsement of derivatives. Factual attribution remains permitted
as provided by the licence.
